2. Using Task Scheduler (More Reliable)

This allows you to run at system startup (before login) or on user logon.

Steps:

Open Task Scheduler (Win + S → search Task Scheduler).

Click Create Task (not "Basic Task").

Under General:

Give it a name (e.g., "Run Node Script").

Select "Run whether user is logged on or not" if you want it to run in background.

Check "Run with highest privileges" (avoids permission issues).

Under Triggers → New:

Choose At log on (or At startup if you want it even before login).

Under Actions → New:

Action: Start a program.

Program/script: node

Add arguments: index.js

Start in: C:\path\to\your\project

Save → Enter your password if prompted.

✅ This will run your Node.js script every time Windows boots/logs in.